old peaks  and will drive many more seeking a warm  bed and a blanket to shelters  but for people like ceni the hard  reality is that surviving the cold at  the moment  is a bigger concern than surviving the  virus  celebrating christmas eve for the around  2 million orthodox christians in germany  it's something of a challenge during  covet lockdown  take the serbian orthodox church of  saint sava  in dusseldorf a year ago thousands of  believers came here to worship  then they didn't have to register but  now the church needs to be able to  contact them if a coronavirus outbreak  occurs  this time only a few dozen worshipers  can take part in the service outside  and a similar number inside the church  [Music]  we have to keep the people safe none of  us may be infected in the church  we have to take care of each other  social distancing face masks no hugging  nor any kissing of the icons as is  common practice in orthodox churches  it's important that we abide by the laws  of the state  at the same time we have to do what god  expects of us  and that is to take care of each other  and to show love to one another  and to be considerate  the choir has also been reduced to just  a few singers  the faithful show their understanding  for the security measures  [Music]  unfortunately this is what we are living  with now we have to make the best of it  but we still have to come here and pray  the custom on christmas eve includes  lighting the so-called bagnak  an oak tree it's a reminder of the fire  that warmth the place where christ was  born  but the authorities have forbidden that  this year too at least the faithful are  allowed to light candles to commemorate  the dead  and to pray for the health of their  families  it's certainly a different christmas eve  this year but some of the traditions  have survived  let's take a look at other developments  in the pandemic  the united states has set another daily  record for new infections  with almost three hundred thousand new  cases and more than  three thousand six hundred deaths  reported on friday  australia's third largest city of  brisbane has entered a three-day  lockdown  after the emergence of a variant first  detected in britain  officials say it was contracted by a  cleaner at a quarantine facility  no community transmissions have been  reported  a new study published in the lancet  medical journal says most people  hospitalized with coronavirus  still have symptoms after six months the  most common ones are fatigue and muscle  weakness  but also sleeping difficulties  you
 

